# Selenium Java Automation

A collection of my Selenium WebDriver practice programs using Java.

## Technologies
- Java 21
- Selenium WebDriver
- Maven
- TestNG
- Eclipse IDE

## Concepts Practiced
- Web element locators
- Alerts
- Dynamic dropdowns
- Static dropdowns
- Auto-suggestions
- Window handling
- Browser interactions

## Project Structure

- `src/intro/` — Selenium practice programs
- `src/level2/` — Additional practice exercises
- `pom.xml` — Maven dependencies and build configuration

## How to Run

1. Clone this repository.
2. Import the project into Eclipse as an existing Maven project.
3. Allow Maven to download the dependencies.
4. Open a Java class containing a Selenium example.
5. Run the class as a Java application.

## Purpose

This repository documents my progress in learning browser automation
and building practical test automation skills.
